{"timestamp": "2026-02-04 18:17:58.863458", "event": "llm_start", "messages": "content='Based on the diagnosis report: ### Troubleshooting Diagnosis Report\\n\\n#### Network Description\\nThe network is an SDN star topology with one central switch (switch_0) and multiple edge switches (switch_1, switch_2, switch_3, switch_4). Hosts (host_1, host_2, host_3, host_4) are connected to edge switches, and all devices share a single access subnet (10.0.0.0/24). The SDN controller operates at 20.0.0.100 and manages the switches via OpenFlow.\\n\\n#### Observations\\n1. **Host Reachability Results**:\\n   - **host_1**:\\n     - Unable to reach **host_2** (status: unknown).\\n     - Unable to reach **host_3** (status: unknown).\\n     - Unable to reach **host_4** (status: unknown).\\n   - **host_2**:\\n     - Unable to reach **host_1** (status: unknown).\\n     - Successfully reached **host_3** with 0% packet loss and average RTT of 10.595 ms.\\n     - Successfully reached **host_4** with 0% packet loss and average RTT of 10.753 ms.\\n   - **host_3**:\\n     - Unable to reach **host_1** (status: unknown).\\n     - Successfully reached **host_2** with 0% packet loss and average RTT of 10.595 ms.\\n     - Unable to reach **host_4** (status: unknown).\\n   - **host_4**:\\n     - Unable to reach **host_1** (status: unknown).\\n     - Successfully reached **host_2** with 0% packet loss and average RTT of 10.753 ms.\\n     - Unable to reach **host_3** (status: unknown).\\n\\n2. **Anomalies Detected**:\\n   - **host_1** appears to be isolated, as it cannot communicate with any other host.\\n   - **host_3** and **host_4** can only communicate with **host_2**, but not with each other or **host_1**.\\n   - **host_2** is reachable from **host_3** and **host_4**, indicating partial connectivity in the network.\\n\\n#### Findings\\n- The network exhibits abnormal behavior, with several hosts unable to communicate with others. This suggests potential issues with:\\n  - The central switch (switch_0) or its connections to edge switches.\\n  - The OpenFlow configuration or SDN controller communication.\\n  - Misconfigured or faulty edge switches (switch_1, switch_3, switch_4).\\n\\n- The successful communication between **host_2**, **host_3**, and **host_4** indicates that some paths in the network are functional, but the overall connectivity is compromised.\\n\\n#### Next Steps\\nFurther investigation is required to:\\n1. Verify the configuration and operational status of the central switch (switch_0).\\n2. Check the OpenFlow connection between switches and the SDN controller.\\n3. Inspect the edge switches (switch_1, switch_3, switch_4) for potential misconfigurations or faults.\\n\\nThis concludes the initial diagnostic report., please provide the submission. Do not submit if no report available.' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={} id='e2421335-24da-4d32-ba25-00006407182f'", "model": {"lc": 1, "type": "constructor", "id": ["langchain", "chat_models", "openai", "ChatOpenAI"], "kwargs": {"model_name": "kt-gpt-oss-rh014", "temperature": 0.0, "openai_api_key": {"lc": 1, "type": "secret", "id": ["OPENAI_API_KEY"]}, "openai_api_base": "https://dev.kora.kt.co.kr/v2", "request_timeout": 180.0, "max_retries": 2}, "name": "ChatOpenAI"}}
